# Agent and AI tooling. All of it is local configuration for whatever
# assistant a contributor happens to use, and none of it describes this
# library. Ignored as a category rather than file by file, so a new
# tool's dotfile does not land in a commit before anyone notices it.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.aider*
.gsd/

# Harness shims that intercept rg/test on Windows. These were committed by an
# auto-commit, hardcoded a personal path to .gsd/agent/bin, and read a file
# .gsd/ already ignores - so they could never work from a clone. Named here
# because they sit at the repo root and under scripts/, where the .gsd/
# directory ignore above does not reach them.
/rg.exe
/rg.cmd
/test.exe
/test.cmd
scripts/RgShim.cs
scripts/TestShim.cs
scripts/verification_rg_wrapper.py

# roam deploy manifests. Per-machine deployment profiles: SSH hostnames,
# local account names, install paths for whatever fleet the maintainer
# deploys to. Local operational config, not part of the library, and the
# one place in this repo that named real hosts. Nothing in the build or
# CI reads them - the roamfile mention in Directory.Build.targets is a
# comment recording a publish invariant.
roamfile*.yaml
!roamfile.example.yaml

# Investigations that are wholly about debugging a downstream deployment.
# Each cites paths and line numbers in a repository that is not published,
# a host profile that is not published, and crash-dump locations on a
# specific machine; generalizing them line by line would leave documents
# that no longer describe anything.
#
# They no longer live in any checkout of this repository. They were moved to a
# private one, which is also where their own internal citations resolve from.
# These entries stay as a guard: if one is ever copied back in, it does not get
# committed.
#
# The remaining docs/investigations/* are about this library and stay tracked.
docs/investigations/2026-06-06-dcomp-mpo-overlay-video-presenter.md
docs/investigations/2026-06-11-pacing-clock-cadence-and-thread-starvation-perf-survey.md
docs/investigations/2026-06-12-composition-interop-presenter-teardown-deadlock.md

# Generated by csharp-api-outline skill
docs/OUTLINE.md
docs/OUTLINE.internal.md

# roam deploy state (sync manifests + run summaries)
.roam/
